        "text": "It was supposed to be clean. Quiet. One last move before walking away. Instead, it became the moment everything began. Matt understands responsibility. Jake understands anger. Luke understands silence. Jace understands regret far too late. Together, they walk a line between survival and ruin, bound by trust that has not yet been tested—and by choices that will follow them long after the dust settles. Krys Callahan knows what it costs to belong to a family that measures worth in obedience. When she chooses to step away from that life, she steps directly into danger, loyalty, and a future she cannot return from. As law and suspicion close in, alliances are strained and truth refuses to stay buried. What happens next will determine not just who walks away—but who becomes something more. This book exists because of patience, stubbornness, and the refusal to accept easy answers. To the readers who believe stories should feel lived in, not polished smooth—this one is for you."
