        "text": "Susanna worked a few steps away, easing soil around the base of the bean poles with a short hoe. She moved slower than she had earlier in the spring, one hand resting now and then against the curve of her stomach as she worked. For weeks the change had been obvious. Dresses had been let out where they could be. Susanna tired sooner in the afternoons and sat more often on the porch while the others finished the day’s work. Susanna leaned the hoe against one of the poles and thought about it a moment. “Six months, maybe a little more.” She studied the younger woman quietly for a moment. “Have you felt the baby moving much yet?” “Jace got to feel it and I swear I thought that man was gonna cry,” Susanna softly said with a smile. “He her hand lightly against her stomach again. “It was smaller before… I kept thinking maybe I was imagining it but now… It’s real… We’re having a baby.” The sounds of the ranch carried steadily through the warm air. From the barn came the clink of harness as Jake and Matt worked with the team. Somewhere near the well Kai’s voice rose and fell while he followed Rhys through the morning chores."
