        "id": "9-147",
        "text": "She can’t understand why I’d want to go back to a place I walked away from. A place that holds so many bad memories for me. I tell her that yes, there were bad years there. Plenty of them. But there were good ones too. Times when the work was quiet and the land stretched out around me and the only sound was the cattle moving through the grass or the horses shifting in the pasture. I tell her there was never a more peaceful feeling than being out there alone with the herd in the early morning. Eric scowls the minute he hears about it and says he doesn’t want to leave the town where all his friends are. Ethan asks if there will even be other kids around and wants to know if they’ll have to sleep in some old broken house. Elizabeth mostly just watches the rest of us, trying to decide how she’s supposed to feel about it. When Erica starts listing all the reasons it’s a bad idea, Elizabeth crosses her arms and says she doesn’t want to go either."
